    "final_answer": "From the BIPM page “The International System of Units (SI): Defining constants,” using only the seven-row defining-constants table and the page text, the seven defining constants in displayed order, with their symbols, exact numerical values, and SI units, are:\n\n1) Caesium hyperfine frequency\n- Name: caesium hyperfine frequency\n- Symbol: ΔνCs\n- Exact numerical value: 9 192 631 770\n- SI unit: Hz\n\n2) Speed of light in vacuum\n- Name: speed of light in vacuum\n- Symbol: c\n- Exact numerical value: 299 792 458\n- SI unit: m s–1\n\n3) Planck constant\n- Name: Planck constant\n- Symbol: h\n- Exact numerical value: 6.626 070 15 x 10–34\n- SI unit: J s\n\n4) Elementary charge\n- Name: elementary charge\n- Symbol: e\n- Exact numerical value: 1.602 176 634 x 10–19\n- SI unit: C\n\n5) Boltzmann constant\n- Name: Boltzmann constant\n- Symbol: k\n- Exact numerical value: 1.380 649 x 10–23\n- SI unit: J K–1\n\n6) Avogadro constant\n- Name: Avogadro constant\n- Symbol: NA\n- Exact numerical value: 6.022 140 76 x 1023\n- SI unit: mol–1\n\n7) Luminous efficacy of a defined visible radiation\n- Name: luminous efficacy of a defined visible radiation\n- Symbol: Kcd\n- Exact numerical value: 683\n- SI unit: lm W–1\n\nPage statement about the uncertainty of these numerical values (quoted exactly from the visible content):\n- “The numerical values of the seven defining constants have no uncertainty.”\n\nThis satisfies the requirement to report all seven defining constants (with symbol, exact numerical value, and SI unit in the order displayed in the table) and the page’s explicit statement about the uncertainty of those numerical values, without adding or inferring any uncertainty beyond what is stated on the BIPM page.",
